# Data from models: fortify

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

ggplot2's reference page for [`fortify()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/fortify.html)
has no examples, so this notebook says only what the page describes and where Giggly stands.

`fortify()` turns a model or another R object into a data frame, so that ggplot2 can plot it; it
is an S3 generic, with methods for particular classes. The page recommends the `broom` package
instead, which covers a much wider range of objects, and says `fortify()` may be deprecated.
Giggly takes any table as a plot's data: a keyword list of columns, a map of columns or a list of
maps. Not in Giggly yet: `fortify()`.
